BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:13f-deadline-20260814@claude-13f
DTSTAMP:20260729T090000Z
DTSTART:20260814T200000Z
DTEND:20260814T213000Z
SUMMARY:📋 13F Deadline - Q2 2026 holdings
DESCRIPTION:13F Deadline - Q2 2026 holdings\nFriday 14 August 2026\n\nTim
 e\n4:00 PM ET  |  20:00 UTC\n\nFiling deadline for Form 13F covering pos
 itions held on 30 June 2026.\n\nTiming\nFilings trickle in from quarter-
 end onwards\, but the big names cluster in the final hours. EDGAR treats
  submissions after 5:30pm ET as filed the next business day\, so 5:30pm 
 is the effective cut-off and the point at which the data set is complete
 .\n\nWho files\nAny institutional manager with at least $100m in Section
  13(f) securities. No extensions are granted\; late filers are told to s
 ubmit as soon as possible.\n\nWhat you get\nLong US equity positions onl
 y. No shorts\, no bonds\, no cash\, no non-US listings\, and confidentia
 l-treatment requests can hide positions temporarily.\n\nREMEMBER THE LAG
 . A 13F shows positions as of the QUARTER-END date\, not the filing date
  - roughly six weeks stale on arrival. A fund that held something on the
  snapshot date may already be out of it. Good for spotting multi-quarter
  accumulation and understanding a manager's approach\; useless as a shor
 t-term signal.\n\nNote Schedule 13G quarterly amendments share these sam
 e four dates.\n\nNotes\nFriday deadline\, so no weekend roll-forward. Fa
 lls the same day as July retail sales and Michigan sentiment prelim.
CATEGORIES:SEC Filings,13F Deadline
URL:https://www.sec.gov/divisions/investment/13ffaq.htm
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
STATUS:CONFIRMED
END:VEVENT
