SUMMARY:📋 13F Deadline - Q3 2026 holdings
DESCRIPTION:13F Deadline - Q3 2026 holdings\nMonday 16 November 2026\n\nT
 ime\n4:00 PM ET  |  21:00 UTC\n\nFiling deadline for Form 13F covering p
 ositions held on 30 September 2026.\n\nTiming\nFilings trickle in from q
 uarter-end onwards\, but the big names cluster in the final hours. EDGAR
  treats submissions after 5:30pm ET as filed the next business day\, so 
 5:30pm is the effective cut-off and the point at which the data set is c
 omplete.\n\nWho files\nAny institutional manager with at least $100m in 
 Section 13(f) securities. No extensions are granted\; late filers are to
 ld to submit as soon as possible.\n\nWhat you get\nLong US equity positi
 ons only. No shorts\, no bonds\, no cash\, no non-US listings\, and conf
 idential-treatment requests can hide positions temporarily.\n\nREMEMBER 
 THE LAG. A 13F shows positions as of the QUARTER-END date\, not the fili
 ng date - roughly six weeks stale on arrival. A fund that held something
  on the snapshot date may already be out of it. Good for spotting multi-
 quarter accumulation and understanding a manager's approach\; useless as
  a short-term signal.\n\nNote Schedule 13G quarterly amendments share th
 ese same four dates.\n\nNotes\nROLLED FORWARD. The nominal 45-day date i
 s Saturday 14 November\, so the deadline moves to Monday 16 November. If
  your compliance calendar still says the 14th\, it is wrong.
CATEGORIES:SEC Filings,13F Deadline
URL:https://www.sec.gov/divisions/investment/13ffaq.htm
